<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jewish Agency for Israel</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1929</span> · Also known as Jewish Agency for Palestine</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Jewish Agency, founded in 1929 as the Jewish Agency for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palestine">Palestine</a>, was the body recognised under the British mandate to represent the Jewish community in Palestine and advise the authorities. Led from 1935 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david">David</a> Ben-Gurion, it organised immigration, land settlement and diplomacy, and its executive formed the core of Israel's first government in 1948. It continues to work on immigration and links with the diaspora.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jewish-agency-for-israel.jpg" alt="Jewish Agency for Israel" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hagai Agmon-Snir حچاي اچمون-سنير חגי אגמון-שניר · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:TheJewishNationalInstitutionsHouseJerusalemMay062023_02.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
